Windows Server 2022 & Active Directory
Installing VMware, Windows Server 2022, and Active Directory creates a centralized IT environment for managing users, computers, security, authentication, and network resources while improving operational efficiency, scalability, reliability, and access control.

Real-life Problem It Solves in a Company
Centralizes employee account management from one location.
Enables secure user authentication using a single login (Single Sign-On).
Controls access to company files, applications, printers, and shared resources.
Simplifies onboarding and offboarding of employees.
Enforces security policies across all company computers.
Reduces IT administration time through centralized management.
Improves business continuity by managing permissions and backups efficiently.
Provides a virtual environment for testing new systems without affecting production.
Supports enterprise applications such as ERP, CRM, email, and financial systems.
Enhances compliance, auditing, and disaster recovery planning.
Example

A company with 100 employees can use VMware to host Windows Server 2022 as a virtual server. Active Directory allows every employee to log in 
with one company account, automatically access authorized folders, printers, email, and business applications, while IT administrators centrally manage passwords, 
permissions, software deployment, and security policies. This reduces downtime, strengthens security, and improves overall operational efficiency.

